    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Output/s</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output/s as listed by the project staff.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Feasibility studies, detailed engineering designs, and due diligence of identified subprojects completed. 
Progress/Status: Agartala Municipal Corporation identified long list of projects in consultation with various stakeholders. Based on the prioritization matrix AMC finalized shortlist of the projects. Topographic survey have been undertaken and feasibility reports are under finalization.  As on date the key submissions are: (i) inception report, (ii) review reports of infrastructure assessment and investment plan, (iii) review of diagnostic reports, (iv) review reports of the institutional capacity development plan, (v) longlists and shortlists of sector-wise projects, and a preliminary infrastructure assessment report; and (v) draft feasibility reports for drainage has been prepared by consultant. 
In view of the DOE&amp;apos;s letter, state finance department is yet to decide the size of the ensuing loan. State has also requested Government of India for prioritizing Agartala Municipal corporation Project.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Institutional capacity strengthened. 
Progress/Status: PRF consultant has carried out capacity building program in collaboration with TA consultant which is targeted to enhance institutional capacity. A detailed workplan are being developed for output 2. 
PRF consultants has also carried out a need assessment based on which a detailed work plan has been developed. Trainings are being conducted.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
